<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">London</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as City of London</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">London is the capital of the United Kingdom, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-thames">River Thames</a>. Founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/londinium">Londinium</a>, it was a significant city of Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. In the era of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> it became the empire's political and financial centre, with the City of London acting as a hub of global trade, banking and investment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="London" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ilya Grigorik · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:London_Skyline_(125508655).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
